  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Psalms",
    "delineation": "Psalm",
    "number": 55,
    "summary": "David prays morning, noon, and night—He seeks protection and help against his enemies.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Give ear to my prayer, O God; and hide not thyself from my supplication.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:1",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Attend unto me, and hear me: I mourn in my complaint, and make a noise;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "OR moan."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:2",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Because of the voice of the enemy, because of the oppression of the wicked: for they cast iniquity upon me, and in wrath they hate me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:3",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "My heart is sore pained within me: and the terrors of death are fallen upon me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "TG Pain."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Pain.",
            "prettyString": "TG Pain",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Pain",
                "entryId": "tg-pain",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:4",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Fearfulness and trembling are come upon me, and horror hath overwhelmed me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:5",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And I said, Oh that I had wings like a dove! for then would I fly away, and be at rest.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:6",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Lo, then would I wander far off, and remain in the wilderness. Selah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 36
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:7",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "I would hasten my escape from the windy storm and tempest.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 49
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:8",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Destroy, O Lord, and divide their tongues: for I have seen violence and strife in the city.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 78,
            "text": "TG Strife."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 20
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Strife.",
            "prettyString": "TG Strife",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Strife",
                "entryId": "tg-strife",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:9",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Day and night they go about it upon the walls thereof: mischief also and sorrow are in the midst of it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 83
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:10",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Wickedness is in the midst thereof: deceit and guile depart not from her streets.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "TG Guile; Sincere."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 13
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Guile; Sincere.",
            "prettyString": "TG Guile; TG Sincere",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Guile",
                "entryId": "tg-guile",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              },
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Sincere",
                "entryId": "tg-sincere",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:11",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "For it was not an enemy that reproached me; then I could have borne it: neither was it he that hated me that did magnify himself against me; then I would have hid myself from him:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 28
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 71
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 86
          },
          {
            "start": 104,
            "end": 108
          },
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 128
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:12",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "But it was thou, a man mine equal, my guide, and mine acquaintance.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:13",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "We took sweet counsel together, and walked unto the house of God in company.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "OR fellowship."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:14",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Let death seize upon them, and let them go down quick into hell: for wickedness is in their dwellings, and among them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "Num. 16:30."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 30
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 82
          },
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 106
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Num. 16:30.",
            "prettyString": "Numbers 16:30",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "numbers",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 16,
                    "end": 16,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 30,
                        "end": 30
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:15",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "As for me, I will call upon God; and the Lord shall save me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:16",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Evening, and morning, and at noon, will I pray, and cry aloud: and he shall hear my voice.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "TG Prayer."
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "Ps. 13:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Prayer.",
            "prettyString": "TG Prayer",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Prayer",
                "entryId": "tg-prayer",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "raw": "Ps. 13:3.",
            "prettyString": "Psalms 13:3",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "psalms",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 13,
                    "end": 13,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 3,
                        "end": 3
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:17",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "He hath delivered my soul in peace from the battle that was against me: for there were many with me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:18",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "God shall hear, and afflict them, even he that abideth of old. Selah. Because they have no changes, therefore they fear not God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "OR humble."
          },
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 98,
            "text": "Job 10:17."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Job 10:17.",
            "prettyString": "Job 10:17",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "job",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 10,
                    "end": 10,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 17,
                        "end": 17
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:19",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "He hath put forth his hands against such as be at peace with him: he hath broken his covenant.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:20",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "The words of his mouth were smoother than butter, but war was in his heart: his words were softer than oil, yet were they drawn swords.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 9
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 61
          },
          {
            "start": 112,
            "end": 116
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:21",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "Cast thy burden upon the Lord, and he shall sustain thee: he shall never suffer the righteous to be moved.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "Prov. 16:3; Matt. 6:25; 11:28 (28–30); Philip. 4:6."
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "1 Ne. 17:35 (33–38); 22:17."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:22",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 55,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "But thou, O God, shalt bring them down into the pit of destruction: bloody and deceitful men shall not live out half their days; but I will trust in thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 55:23",
